  "notes": {
    "two_measures": "WAS (survey, household incl. private pensions, GB) and NBS (national accounts, household sector net worth, UK) measure different things and DO NOT match; ONS states they are not directly comparable.",
    "was_top10": "WAS top-10% share comes in 2-year rounds; annual values are LINEAR INTERPOLATION (interpolated_top10=true) between round mid-years only; no WAS value outside 2007\u20132021.",
    "was_method_break": "2020\u201322 round (top10 40.7%) uses SCAPE-based pension methodology \u2014 a BREAK vs earlier rounds (43\u201345%). Do not read 45%\u219241% as pure real change.",
    "wid_vs_was": "WID top-10 (~57%) is individual net personal wealth from capitalization methods and is systematically higher than the WAS household survey floor (~43-45%); both are real published numbers.",
    "top1pct": "ONS states top-1% household share = 10% of total wealth (Apr 2020\u2013Mar 2022, prose only). WID-based estimates (Advani/Bangham/Leslie; Wealth Tax Commission) find surveys under-capture the top, so 10% is a floor.",
    "flows_gap": "GAP: no clean annual public wealth-flow (savings vs appreciation) series was assembled. Best flow-adjacent evidence: WAS Table 2.1 shows 2006-08\u21922018-20 growth was driven by private pension wealth (2886\u21926445 \u00a3bn) and net property (3537\u21925458 \u00a3bn); NBS 2024 household net worth rose \u00a3217.7bn, driven by land (+\u00a3176.7bn) i.e. appreciation, not saving. Flagged as honest gap.",
    "projection": "PROJECTION METHOD (honest): for years beyond latest data, do NOT extrapolate the distribution \u2014 hold the last observed WID top-10 share constant with a \u00b11pp uncertainty band (2013\u20132024 series moved within ~1pp of 57); for NBS total, use last-decade CAGR (~3%/yr nominal) with a \u00b12%/yr band, clearly labelled as trend extrapolation, not forecast. Any animated projection must be visually flagged as extrapolated."
  },
  "projection_method_note": "Simple trend extrapolation only, never beyond 2 years, with explicit uncertainty bands and an 'extrapolated' flag in the animation. No causal model."
}